      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T15:46:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There shouldn\u0027t be any factories in the base class. The factories should all be declared/defined in the backend specific classes. Also the factory needs to return an SkContext object.\n\nso we would have things like:\n```\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cSkContext\u003e skcpu::SkContexts::Make(SkContextOptions\u0026);\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cSkContext\u003e skgpu::graphite::SkContexts::Make(SkContextOptions\u0026, GraphiteContextOptions\u0026);\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cSkContext\u003e skgpu::ganesh::SkContexts::Make(SkContextOptions\u0026, GrContextOptions\u0026);\n\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "312f326ff3428d6d4e3b0ced2c1a92534ff2caeb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "455a401a_f3ceb217",
        "filename": "include/core/SkContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 4623515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T17:21:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there\u0027s a misunderstanding. This make is the one mentioned in the design doc (in the Composition vs Inheritance for SkContext section at the bottom). \n\nIt\u0027s meant to replace the SkGraphics::Init function.",
      "parentUuid": "71a35d33_488ef20d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "312f326ff3428d6d4e3b0ced2c1a92534ff2caeb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93b93ffe_d6f50059",
        "filename": "include/core/SkContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T17:33:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe there is a point to have a temporary static function to initialize a global SkContext while migrating to this new API, but then I\u0027d argue that logic should just be inside `SkGraphics::Init()` with the goal that the global SkContext it creates is removed when `SkGraphics::Init()` can be deleted.\n\nLong term, there should not be a static function that initializes globals for `SkContext`. The point of `SkContext` is that it owns everything inside (or inside of the backend subclasses) and does not reach out to globals. Where Chrome or other clients currently initialize Skia globals should go away and they would create and own a `std::unique_ptr\u003cContext\u003e`.  That would be their initialization in the new world (or possible a shared pointer to Context).",
      "parentUuid": "455a401a_f3ceb217",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "312f326ff3428d6d4e3b0ced2c1a92534ff2caeb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e807c16_61876ac1",
        "filename": "include/core/SkContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 4623515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T18:05:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think, for now, we can keep the initialization logic within SkGraphics::Init(). I don\u0027t see anywhere else it could go. \n\nI\u0027ll update this CL that adds the factory methods so that it calls SkGraphics::Init() at first.\n\nhttps://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/1391637",
      "parentUuid": "93b93ffe_d6f50059",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "312f326ff3428d6d4e3b0ced2c1a92534ff2caeb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54a6c2ae_db9d0a0a",
        "filename": "include/core/SkContext.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T18:10:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think during the transition, SkGraphics::Init will end up making the global SkContext object. And then at least all the CPU related calls will be forwarded from our global functions to setting/querying the global SkContext. So in that world the work done today in Init will be move the ctor of SkContext. There are some open questions in this transition phase about how to the gpu contexts will be handled since we can\u0027t easily put them on the global SkContext.",
      "parentUuid": "3e807c16_61876ac1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 23
      },
